      ":question/id": "c8b227a8-149a-5af2-9e48-23b44d592c8a",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x + 2 y - z &=-6 \\\\ - 2 x - 3 y + 2 z &=14 \\\\ 2 x + 3 y - z &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & -6 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 & 14 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & -6 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 & 14 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
